<!-- 1:1 fivem.net Developers Band (.dev + .langs) -->
<section class="dev">
  <div class="text">
    <div class="subtitle">Developers</div>
    <div class="title">Creativity at its best</div>
    <p>
      Build rich gamemodes, custom NUI interfaces, and high-performance multiplayer experiences using the Cfx.re FXServer runtime. Issue your `sv_licenseKey` in NSM Keymaster and publish your server to the live masterlist in seconds.
    </p>
    <div class="action">
      <a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" href="/docs">Documentation</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg" href="/keymaster">Server Keymaster</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg" href="/forum">Developer Forum</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="langs">
  <div class="lang lua">
    <div class="name">Lua</div>
    <div class="desc">Lightweight, fast, and familiar scripting with coroutines and direct GTA V native access.</div>
    <pre><code>CreateThread(function()
  while true do
    Wait(0)
    DrawMarker(2, x, y, z, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0,
      0.0, 180.0, 0.0, 2.0, 2.0, 2.0,
      47, 123, 255, 180, false, true, 2)
  end
end)</code></pre>
  </div>

  <div class="lang cs">
    <div class="name">C#</div>
    <div class="desc">Strongly-typed .NET scripting for complex gamemodes and shared client/server libraries.</div>
    <pre><code>public class MyScript : BaseScript
{
  [Command("car")]
  public async void SpawnCar(int src, List&lt;object&gt; args)
  {
    var hash = (uint)GetHashKey("adder");
    await World.CreateVehicle(hash, Game.PlayerPed.Position);
  }
}</code></pre>
  </div>

  <div class="lang js">
    <div class="name">JavaScript</div>
    <div class="desc">Modern V8 / Node.js runtime with full npm ecosystem support and React/Vue NUI integration.</div>
    <pre><code>RegisterCommand('spawn', async (src, args) =&gt; {
  const model = args[0] || 'zentorno';
  emitNet('nsm:spawnVehicle', src, model);
}, false);</code></pre>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 1:1 fivem.net 7-Item Anchored FAQ (.faq) -->
<section class="faq">
  <h1>FAQ</h1>
  <div class="faq-grid">
    <article id="faq1">
      <h2><a href="#faq1">Will I get banned from GTA:Online for playing NSM?</a></h2>
      <p>
        No. NSM does not modify or touch your Grand Theft Auto V installation files at all, and runs inside an isolated application directory with its own network stack.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article id="faq2">
      <h2><a href="#faq2">Why can't I find any servers?</a></h2>
      <p>
        Make sure <code>NSM-Masterlist.exe</code> is running and that your FXServer has a valid <code>sv_licenseKey</code> issued from <a href="/keymaster">NSM Keymaster</a> and announces heartbeats to the masterlist.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article id="faq3">
      <h2><a href="#faq3">What are the requirements for running NSM?</a></h2>
      <p>
        A legitimate installation of Grand Theft Auto V on Windows 10 or Windows 11 (64-bit) via Steam, Epic Games, or Rockstar Games Launcher.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article id="faq4">
      <h2><a href="#faq4">Does NSM cost anything?</a></h2>
      <p>
        No! Downloading the client, creating an account, browsing servers, and issuing server license keys in <a href="/keymaster">Keymaster</a> are completely free.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article id="faq5">
      <h2><a href="#faq5">How do I host a server and get a license key?</a></h2>
      <p>
        Sign in and open <a href="/keymaster">Keymaster</a> to generate a <code>cfxk_nsm_...</code> license key. Add <code>set sv_licenseKey "cfxk_nsm_..."</code> to your <code>server.cfg</code> and start your server.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article id="faq6">
      <h2><a href="#faq6">How does signing in inside NSM.exe work?</a></h2>
      <p>
        You can sign in directly inside <code>NSM.exe</code>'s account flyout with your NSM username/email and password, or click Link Account to authorize via the website.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

